hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3034","Narrated to us ‘Imrān ibn Mūsā al-Qazzāz – on the authority of ‘Abd al-Wārith ibn Sa‘īd – who narrated to us Abū al-Tayyāh – who narrated to us Mūsā ibn Salamah al-Hudhalī who said:\n\nMu‘tamir (i.e., performing ‘umrah) set out with Sinān ibn Salamah. When we arrived at al-Baṭḥā’, I said, “Let us go to Ibn ‘Abbās so we may speak with him.”\nSinān said to Ibn ‘Abbās, “Indeed, my mother is in the city (al-Miṣr), and I go out on these military expeditions. If I free a slave in her place, will it suffice for her?”\nIbn ‘Abbās replied, “Shall I not tell you of something more amazing than that? I ordered the wife of Sinān ibn ‘Abd Allāh al-Juhanī to ask the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) for me: her mother died and she had not performed ḥajj. Would it suffice for her mother to perform ḥajj on her behalf?”\nHe (the Prophet ﷺ) said, “Yes. If her mother had a debt, would she have paid it on her behalf? Would it not have sufficed? Then let her perform ḥajj on behalf of her mother.”\n\n\n\nCHAPTER:"
"3035","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn ‘Abdah: narrated to us Hammād ibn Zayd: on the authority of Abū al-Tayyāḥ: on the authority of Mūsā ibn Salamah who said:\nI heard Ibn ‘Abbās (RA) say that a man from the Juhaynah tribe said:\n“O Messenger of Allāh, my father died while he was an old man who had not performed Hajj, or was unable to perform Hajj.”\nHe (ﷺ) said:\n“Perform Hajj on behalf of your father.”\n\nCHAPTER:"
